#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/id #uuid "2d4b2c66-5600-5712-8ec9-3d7325b247c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-11348" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 4x^3  \\: \\mathrm{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR = \\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the $z$-axis, and the line $z = 4-y$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} 4x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}} 4x^3 \\, \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}4{x}^{3}\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{4}]_{x=0}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{(\\sqrt{y})}^{4}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate this double integral over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/3c/3c8712fa0a30ad94f503efe5e080ee89f83eb21f19fba45033bbedeab08ac816.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y}{y}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{y}^{2}z]_{z=0}^{z=4-y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{y}^{2}(4-y)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}4{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(64-0)-\\frac{1}{4}(256-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{64}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133476 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "295afdb2-2e90-5f1a-8830-d3886d99fbad" :question/math-academy-id "e-11349" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_D \\left[ \\int_{0}^{z} \\dfrac{\\cos (2y)}{1-y} \\,\\textrm{d}x \\right] \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD = \\left\\{ (y,z) \\, : \\, 0 \\leq y \\leq \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 2\\sqrt{1-y} \\right\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}(z-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\sqrt{1-y}}\\frac{z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2\\sqrt{1-y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}{1-y}(\\frac{4(1-y)}{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)]_{y=0}^{y=\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "ad3e88cb-f213-509b-93c5-3fc529d617c0" :question/math-academy-id "e-12369" :question/problem "![](images/fc/fc19dd4415663ab027e0fc386d4c5bc81a28c1bc26d5f6cf2083f4f4228a4dea.png)\n\n \n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n$\\displaystyle \\iiint\\limits_R 12z^2 \\: \\mathrm{d}V$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/f2/f25c393f10c35ffd9b4fa91cdf672a516cf6cff974a8aa563d350619a64b79bd.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/14/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 3-y-z \\big\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\iiint \\limits_{R}  12z^2  \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{3-y-z}  12z^2  \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}12{z}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}12{z}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}12{z}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=3-y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}12{z}^{2}(3-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(36{z}^{2}-12y{z}^{2}-12{z}^{3})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[12{z}^{3}-4y{z}^{3}-3{z}^{4}]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12-4y-3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9-4y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9-4y)\\,dy & =[9y-2{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(9-2)-0 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133484 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/id #uuid "b51667a8-f48a-59a2-b09e-59c6fcad5507" :question/math-academy-id "e-12398" :question/problem "Find the missing limits in the repeated integral below\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V\n= \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \n\\int_{\\ast}^{\\ast} \nf(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\: \\mathrm{d}z \\: \\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region defined as\n\n$$\nR=\\left\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y}, \\: -2 \\leq x \\leq ye^{z+2} \\right\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z)  \\: : \\: (y,z) \\in D, \\: u_1(y,z) \\leq x \\leq u_2(y,z) \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\iiint\\limits_{R} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm d V = \\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[\\int_{u_1(y,z)}^{u_2(y,z)} f(x,y,z)\\,\\textrm{d}x \\right]\\,\\textrm d A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu_1(y,z) = -2, \\qquad u_2(y,z)  = ye^{z+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\iiint \\limits_{R} f(x,y,z) \\: \\textrm{d}V \n= \n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\left[ \\int_{-2}^{ye^{z+2}} f(x,y,z) \\: \\mathrm{d}x \\right] \\mathrm{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD =\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 4, \\: -y^2 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{y} \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}[{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dz\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}{\\int }_{-2}^{y{e}^{z+2}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527947 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03b0b981-db99-5320-9dc6-a1d8b790b501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527313} {:answer/id #uuid "55cdfdaf-a5f8-5b18-936d-a75973001c72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527471} {:answer/id #uuid "9af24a3e-e04a-58ef-a429-924564378f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527628} {:answer/id #uuid "d466183b-9be0-5365-834f-40f6ffa3832c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527737} {:answer/id #uuid "d99c0d9e-50cc-59d3-ae76-b760eb2c7b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d466183b-9be0-5365-834f-40f6ffa3832c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527737} :answer-field/id #uuid "910f7d09-fcda-54a5-88cc-37189d89f510" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5bfcca82-6474-54bc-a5e0-2e4323bbf96b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161546" :question/problem "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,(3y-z)^{2}\\le x\\le {e}^{y+4z}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=(3y-z)^{2}\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={e}^{y+4z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{(3y-z)^{2}}^{{e}^{y+4z}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278550 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "131cd702-d3db-5a3f-aa72-90940a18623b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dy]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275653} {:answer/id #uuid "1c17d300-8e1d-5b91-8a26-8954a3aeb799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275736} {:answer/id #uuid "a675af5d-f74d-565b-a333-9e8e7c402d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276977} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4a06b8-9c6a-5f4e-98d6-6a92e46e36af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}[{∬}_{D}f(x,y,z)\\,dA]dz" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277690} {:answer/id #uuid "ff5ce57d-6f46-58a7-8999-eceb95753252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277721}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff5ce57d-6f46-58a7-8999-eceb95753252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277721} :answer-field/id #uuid "094e0128-f9bc-5e60-971e-e6ff9d407f85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "587a8773-2afe-542a-990e-6aafa5beb6ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-161548" :question/problem "Consider the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,-3\\le x\\le 5{y}^{4}+2\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is some finite region in the $yz$-plane. Then,\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1b49704bf6d5837a18d8b5dbb8b420d430d5e3881507540fb62a45cf1f6ce52f.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-3\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=5{y}^{4}+2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-3}^{5{y}^{4}+2}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bc60df2-8730-5e1e-bb8a-e55cbc507546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527367} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd647e1-d76e-51a0-9ccd-a0bd017494ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527481} {:answer/id #uuid "6214fdd5-48a4-5599-acaa-959b2a1436e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527491} {:answer/id #uuid "90d7a5d8-344b-556d-9123-9417e82aa3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527591} {:answer/id #uuid "91f4c10c-f73b-509c-9c7a-360f4a6c7f87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6214fdd5-48a4-5599-acaa-959b2a1436e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527491} :answer-field/id #uuid "332dc5a3-6077-5a95-b9d8-7163745f52d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00568ac8-b77a-5f52-9484-f19c655aa6d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161558" :question/problem "![](images/57/5780b9e67272fdd78a24aab108fb9c672ee76ff2d62376991cea03c7efaa81fe.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/24/240cc6d74e266579aa848be820fd0014672aa0654f079c079472a896ad44c5fe.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y+2z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/27/27862dcc3effe5801c812f5c8944c0134d13bb38f99d337b0a4e20e9ff815639.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y+2z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{z}{12}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y+2z}\\frac{z}{12}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{z}{12}[x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{z}{12}(4-y+2z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{12}(4z-yz+2{z}^{2})\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{12}{[2{z}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}y{z}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{12}(18-\\frac{9}{2}y+18)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(3-\\frac{3}{8}y)\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(3-\\frac{3}{8}y)\\,dy & ={[3y-\\frac{3}{16}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=4} \\\\  & =(12-3)-0 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278554 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b60f63f-433f-54e7-9f87-f725cb0d657e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276295} {:answer/id #uuid "92c0a635-408b-5bd1-9ac1-7efe6bdb0e62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276805} {:answer/id #uuid "bd54688b-55d1-598f-b4b7-061007d0032d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277164} {:answer/id #uuid "c64b5112-2962-5c4f-84ed-2f68903e4b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277243} {:answer/id #uuid "f35cfe49-e6e9-5ce8-8ba6-5d6cd60fb936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c64b5112-2962-5c4f-84ed-2f68903e4b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277243} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6dfb508-76d9-5717-9115-0d19ca58e6d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2982d5e-855b-5753-9807-1b56cd50c77d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161561" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le \\sqrt{4-2y}\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z}4xz\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[2z{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2z({z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-2y}}2{z}^{3}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{4-2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(\\sqrt{4-2y)})^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(4-2y)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{2}(16-16y+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}8-8y+2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8y-4{y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =16-16+\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527997 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213676f8-b331-59a5-91dc-1bbb59780c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527382} {:answer/id #uuid "2576b112-e737-588e-bcf0-2d79e0be3dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}+y+z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527393} {:answer/id #uuid "56d0d569-69e7-5401-aef9-9822b9b489fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527473} {:answer/id #uuid "6c807fef-55cf-5829-b452-0803cc158708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527513} {:answer/id #uuid "b328e717-67f5-5280-9783-f298a5c3a64b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}-y-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56d0d569-69e7-5401-aef9-9822b9b489fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527473} :answer-field/id #uuid "62838ed0-438a-5299-a107-f9a335821ea7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3a2b2c0-5dc8-56bd-94aa-3a2ccfd9aff3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161562" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le z,\\,2\\le z\\le 3,\\,-y-z\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{4}\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-y-z,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+{z}^{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le z,\\,2\\le z\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{z}[{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{-2}^{z}{\\int }_{-y-z}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{4}}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=-2+z=z-2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2222d75d-c999-5cef-bcdd-21fd712d7967" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275784} {:answer/id #uuid "8f11ed39-68a9-5931-9d16-2e3abceb2ce2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276774} {:answer/id #uuid "af53cc19-10ff-5824-a8a2-6cddf6b69797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+\\sqrt{y+z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277046} {:answer/id #uuid "bb61f8c2-b846-58f6-b5a3-d64d1aa38cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277141} {:answer/id #uuid "ffecb9c8-dc3b-560f-a18c-66bafff8cf64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-\\sqrt{y+z}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb61f8c2-b846-58f6-b5a3-d64d1aa38cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277141} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f350725-0e4e-580b-a33d-a775ccb274cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277819}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ac74bdd-4f55-52a9-8415-18543bfb88ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-161564" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5,\\,-\\sqrt{y+z}\\le x\\le 4\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-\\sqrt{y+z},\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-z\\le y\\le 1,\\,4\\le z\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{4}^{5}{\\int }_{-z}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{y+z}}^{4}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=4+5=9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133924 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a22ed84a-4b6f-53b3-8336-bf592aed8686" :knowledge-point/title "Representing a Triple Integral as a Mixed or Repeated Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "505c7e4b-7779-5b74-903b-e90c8023eae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276196} {:answer/id #uuid "68c320d3-66a6-5afb-b396-ac305424f7cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+2z-2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276418} {:answer/id #uuid "a13f06d6-3684-5189-9263-82c1a846137d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡z+\\pi -8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276930} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dd82f1-56c8-5209-97a0-5e47bf0e59c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}+2z-2y-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277000} {:answer/id #uuid "f13dcfdf-9280-5fd0-9cca-4509d35df4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sin}^{2}⁡z-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "505c7e4b-7779-5b74-903b-e90c8023eae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276196} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f08b750-8569-5722-9291-eebf799c1107" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29632302-5883-5021-9de6-855ebf0325c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161566" :question/problem "The triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz\n$$\n\nis defined over the type II region $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi ,\\,-2y-1\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+2z\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "A type II region in three-dimensional space can be written as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{u}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {u}_{2}(y,z)\\}.\n$$\n\nA typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a9/a905e1f60fb0aa865c071fcbccbfecb30dcac7a74b4b647d24a40f4c89ff1935.png)\n\n \n\nIf $R$ is a type II region, we can express the triple integral of $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ as a mixed integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}(y,z)=-2y-1,\\,{u}_{2}(y,z)={y}^{2}+2z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our triple integral can be written as\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nNow, the region $D$ is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-8\\le y\\le {sin}^{2}⁡z,\\,0\\le z\\le \\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by expressing the double integral over $D$ as a repeated integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}[{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx]dy\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-8}^{{sin}^{2}⁡z}{\\int }_{-2y-1}^{{y}^{2}+2z}f(x,y,z)\\,dx\\,dy\\,dz.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\na+b=0+\\pi =\\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64b93f40-e571-5114-b903-9dd492e51b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527497} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb11349-f33e-5227-8226-abc8119f362b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527514} {:answer/id #uuid "7b6af685-0917-5dc1-883d-148ee49f787b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527538} {:answer/id #uuid "a64dc4e7-e9b1-5616-8dbc-3c99ab7b4f6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527650} {:answer/id #uuid "b7557761-3d9b-5307-8631-4113b0f39d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64b93f40-e571-5114-b903-9dd492e51b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aaf8073-fd00-580d-ae0f-671cb6cc5fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0884b1e2-1bba-5f2c-8a6a-f7af258e16fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-161568" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{y}^{y+z}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=y}^{x=y+z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(y+z)^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz+{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[y{z}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{4}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(16-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527988 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390a0a3f-8045-51e4-9e9a-3692b030cba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{24}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527421} {:answer/id #uuid "45156b6e-6526-56b2-a152-2e340488d5e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527440} {:answer/id #uuid "72cceeab-ae35-5169-ba9f-38c49406c64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527523} {:answer/id #uuid "85994e10-7a1c-5399-818a-6d0eb148e72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527566} {:answer/id #uuid "a03f33e4-9c17-5d89-ba8f-89c5877bca3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527638}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85994e10-7a1c-5399-818a-6d0eb148e72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527566} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e440dfe-c51c-5a5e-a6b4-025b490904aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bf9108b7-225d-5060-8e6a-417eee5fc631" :question/math-academy-id "q-161572" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le z\\le y\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{1-y-z}24y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}24y[x]_{x=0}^{x=1-y-z}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y(1-y-z)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}24y-24{y}^{2}-24yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}24(y-{y}^{2})-24yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})[z]_{z=0}^{z=y}-12y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24(y-{y}^{2})y-12{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}24{y}^{2}-36{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[8{y}^{3}-9{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1/2} \\\\  & =8(\\frac{1}{8}-0)-9(\\frac{1}{16}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a14f67b0-77e7-5ad2-bed1-6f40742b91fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130925} {:answer/id #uuid "aab2d86c-e157-5e56-8d6e-acbe88ccf262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130926} {:answer/id #uuid "ef563ce8-107d-527c-92e3-beb40d14a996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130927} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7d0390-01a3-59b0-a991-6ed1293f7ba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130928} {:answer/id #uuid "5cc9f6ca-4a76-5b98-9134-af437d186875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef563ce8-107d-527c-92e3-beb40d14a996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130927} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e843666-e94f-5e5d-a692-2cd9aab8f479" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1f663fe3-dd5b-577a-af75-1af60254b416" :question/math-academy-id "q-161574" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y{z}^{2}}\\frac{12}{z}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,1\\le z\\le \\sqrt{2y}\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y{z}^{2}}\\frac{12}{z}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{12}{z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=y{z}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{12}{z}(y{z}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{2y}}12yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[6y{z}^{2}]_{z=1}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6y((\\sqrt{2y})^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}6y(2y-1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}12{y}^{2}-6y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4{y}^{3}-3{y}^{2}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =4(8-1)-3(4-1) \\\\  & =19\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527982 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19275c3c-3b62-52d9-8834-c801d03c7960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527360} {:answer/id #uuid "342d4137-1b3b-5d92-9976-ded77f49bf51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527414} {:answer/id #uuid "96c9ccd5-1b78-5c4c-a828-b878bf42e2df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527609} {:answer/id #uuid "97e51b4b-6a3a-5ba4-9dac-c09d0bff420b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527614} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6d38d4-3b20-5c92-a589-3094afbbedb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19275c3c-3b62-52d9-8834-c801d03c7960" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527360} :answer-field/id #uuid "837c4e53-1331-51f5-bdfe-c0ba2752cec2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b38931ca-6fb1-5b3c-b019-b45d2fe482a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-161578" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V\n$$\n\nwhere $R$ is the type II region given by \n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 4-y-z\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{4-y-z}2\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[2x]_{x=0}^{x=4-y-z}dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2(4-y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[8z-2yz-{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}8-2y-1\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}7-2y\\,dy & ={[7y-{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =7-1 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528005 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0282d2f5-2a53-58db-a10f-e26b85fe6f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527310} {:answer/id #uuid "3fcfb3a6-bd6a-5f81-b119-ffca2871d580" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527432} {:answer/id #uuid "806d8ac7-8b82-599c-9872-2d84cc0bb623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527556} {:answer/id #uuid "8768788c-5a1c-5056-8877-7d8c7cb5dc7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527572} {:answer/id #uuid "9fd9e948-6464-58a2-a0f2-d61ae7071f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fd9e948-6464-58a2-a0f2-d61ae7071f1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{72}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527637} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a706466-bb58-58a9-b091-d4ba42a7541f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e31a3154-dd92-51e0-baa5-7e556d0b4865" :question/math-academy-id "q-161580" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le y+z\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2xyz\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y+z}2xyz\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}yz[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=y+z}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz(y+z)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}yz({y}^{2}+2yz+{z}^{2})\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/59/5974f852ba8dcaf9e6c4d6323709987c590e2f739524e012545738bc4bb842b0.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}{y}^{3}z+2{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+y{z}^{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}{z}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y{z}^{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}\\cdot {y}^{2}+\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{2}\\cdot {y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{4}y\\cdot {y}^{4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{17}{12}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{5}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}{[\\frac{1}{6}{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{12}(\\frac{1}{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03ae4bcf-d3f1-5dfe-ad4a-107b992c5ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275513} {:answer/id #uuid "5db782bc-2b40-59fd-9dc7-61af5a16a051" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276313} {:answer/id #uuid "650304c1-ef1f-5e6c-84cf-788bbd4294dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276384} {:answer/id #uuid "a800cdd3-3aad-5551-9a4a-388037da32de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276994} {:answer/id #uuid "bd74c20a-04a9-5742-a624-7f4d5b1dcb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd74c20a-04a9-5742-a624-7f4d5b1dcb3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277168} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6d4669-2187-519d-a532-0e68a234114c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277887}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "40c7ad15-9d9f-5fe8-85c1-e6adcf3df389" :question/math-academy-id "q-161583" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le yz\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z={y}^{2}$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2x\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{yz}2x\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(yz)^{2}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/ac/acb173db9d28ed8b38e63c7bc365c20e5755aeb1af3f6340e7b9229a4b49101d.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}{z}^{3}]}_{z=0}^{z={y}^{2}}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{2}({y}^{6}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{8}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{9}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{9}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278566 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f8e4b7b-e3ec-5734-95c4-f3c524afc21a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{34}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276189} {:answer/id #uuid "a467a30d-d76f-5115-be5a-fe13677662bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{72}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276958} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a811da-034c-53e9-92a9-fa69054f8cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277236} {:answer/id #uuid "cfccbb0d-2768-5c28-9ab0-be5dd2b5e9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{67}{92}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277317} {:answer/id #uuid "d8cd8db2-d1c9-5016-968d-3ce6bf214109" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{79}{100}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5a811da-034c-53e9-92a9-fa69054f8cf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{61}{105}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277236} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb0ee147-a553-542c-8e10-1d6e3f554db7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a816d812-5042-53f7-abc8-46b6718aff74" :question/math-academy-id "q-161585" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le {y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axis, the line $y=1$ and the parabola $z=-{y}^{2}$ in the fourth quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}[x]_{x=0}^{x={y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/38/38ea49a6fae41574107b2ba68a578586a306cf43d419d4de5699dcfa009137c2.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{-{y}^{2}}^{0}{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}+1\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[({y}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-{y}^{2}}^{z=0}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1)((0-(-{y}^{2}))+\\frac{1}{3}(0-{(-{y}^{2})}^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+1){y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{6}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{5}{y}^{5}+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{21}{y}^{7}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{61}{105}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278567 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72e3970d-6049-556a-bf73-74d44a6c57c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276518} {:answer/id #uuid "745b2de0-7f97-542e-9b6a-37e43cae796f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276529} {:answer/id #uuid "77f6c800-74c2-5cdb-a91f-54845eccf174" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276564} {:answer/id #uuid "9f9abd94-8eae-51c3-bbdf-96adcdff08c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276914} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4919ec-dc6d-572d-8ced-ce05872a77d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277131}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72e3970d-6049-556a-bf73-74d44a6c57c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276518} :answer-field/id #uuid "f088e059-56d3-5859-8349-448073079bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278149}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5d288958-0f39-531c-abbd-563a70ab640a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161589" :question/problem "![](images/d5/d5690bff5819d72cc9d49016c119dc79f62f4d766c142a43a89df196ce9f2335.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/24/2427e053c0e2d808b32db5d7fedf81365e7e50f0b3f2dc61598ad1795394686e.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/14/145f0d494ffe24de84e3a289b3a7316d3f4933f193d734aed118609f7fb9f94f.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}{y}^{2}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{2}(2+2y-z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-{y}^{2}z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[2{y}^{2}z+2{y}^{3}z-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2{y}^{3}\\,dy & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186528011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17b4332a-b7f8-5171-8c97-496f5d3f6318" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527355} {:answer/id #uuid "34a3ea0d-a9f1-5107-b26b-9a8264ffde7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527415} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e002bf-b18b-54ee-a07d-976d9e512509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527670} {:answer/id #uuid "cc4e3fad-bad0-5e05-9133-2df8bbdea95f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3y\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527718} {:answer/id #uuid "e074fa5f-5aa5-57c2-83a8-4980654a8ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527752}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0e002bf-b18b-54ee-a07d-976d9e512509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527670} :answer-field/id #uuid "e767016c-6faf-58ba-ac6e-34fede0af637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f2d33e33-cbe1-5877-8ed6-72bcb8e7fff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161690" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca994203c4a3889949e3452f48ea3f7295a152c5d9d4c809758f152d7115cedf.png)\n\nGiven that $R$ is the type II region shown above, \n${∭}_{R}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V=$" :question/worked-solution "For a type II region $R$ with projection $D$ onto the $yz$-plane, the triple integral of a continuous function $f(x,y,z)$ over $R$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(y,z)}^{{u}_{2}(y,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe consider the region $R$ as a type II region enclosed between the back surface $x={u}_{1}(y,z)=1$ and the front surface $x={u}_{2}(y,z)=2.$\n\n![](images/a3/a39d7a27f20283b6e6814db926801f16e3e2cb42c7fe16487350b536d3b63d3c.png)\n\nSo, the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,1\\le x\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ as a type I *plane* region in the $yz$-plane with the upper curve\n\n$$\nz=1-(y-1)^{2}.\n$$\n\n![](images/50/5058493860a1c4d919e3cd6786bb1aca156ae83d47f766c087e351e9764929c4.png)\n\nHence, $D=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 1-(y-1)^{2}\\}.$\n\nTherefore, we write the triple integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∭}_{R}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}V & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡z[{x}^{2}]_{x=1}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1-(y-1)^{2}}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡z\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281323 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f863192-f157-5fb8-942d-593165f6be17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279007} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0a52c4-85e6-5e49-87e7-389cbb36adbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279138} {:answer/id #uuid "50f21f17-6e6a-547f-9424-2ed97e19e1ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279330} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3de7a1-dfce-5742-8880-f5852e9d512f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279956} {:answer/id #uuid "ccc2f76c-4d6a-5867-b8af-3f6282d7d40f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e0a52c4-85e6-5e49-87e7-389cbb36adbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279138} :answer-field/id #uuid "736232dd-927d-57e3-adc3-ed1ba5cd49e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "90f67d54-9024-5f72-8cbf-c5f497fb6e8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-161783" :question/problem "![](images/3f/3fe3ec24f8f8006f22bde8ba2dc39fd3cd3f73668b06f8ea4a74e4ed5206a193.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/2a/2a20f2651c24e48871028b44fe61da4600d632481877ef32ccdfd3241262a53b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/1b/1ba7c02f254313a73a813e4e43c44c25523ce77dd47e594a1db3b412a6bd5c3d.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 5-y-\\frac{z}{2}\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{5-y-z/2}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=5-y-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{10-2y-z}(5-y-\\frac{z}{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{z}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=4}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\,dy & =[2y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =6-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281324 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133922 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e612d4ba-b772-5f56-a031-fdfc05d63221" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56db55ba-db05-567a-9988-071184b844d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279386} {:answer/id #uuid "688f55f5-366d-5010-ab2b-a189e5f23bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279543} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf90354-3814-59d5-a7cf-c0bc9a3254d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279848} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a47d8f-8a5c-5150-8c7d-8102990223cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280724} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1c3683-c4dd-5443-82b2-d8994d7dbb7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "688f55f5-366d-5010-ab2b-a189e5f23bc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279543} :answer-field/id #uuid "7566d184-eeca-5394-8d91-0aadcdbc31b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78eec2a4-7ee5-59eb-8402-37f965ae8bd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161784" :question/problem "![](images/ca/ca49b92d602d04a73dc7ab9936d601654bd293ce3fb7950372ac86155875aca3.png)\n\nEvaluate the triple integral \n${∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dV$\nover the region $R,$ shown above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/00/0008ba406cfe8a5b61d683a6854260897cb441752a5333add281ab1279e31b0b.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bbe6b6b897e5d53421080ae8e8b9dc49f2ea1b7e135f8426ee3f11af01cc2401.png)\n\nHence, we can express the region $R$ as\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le 2-\\frac{y}{3}+z\\}\n$$\n\nAs a result, by writing down our triple integral as a repeated integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x$, treating $y$ and $z$ as constants: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3+z}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}\\,dx]dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{6-y+3z}(2-\\frac{y}{3}+z)\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz\\,dy & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}{[z]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{3}(3)\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\,dy & =[y]_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134268 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133914 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90adf237-9627-55f1-8f90-8fbc4acf02fc" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Triple Integral Over a Type II Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dfa63d1-2a3c-5f98-ac88-3e5a9c4a677a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324472} {:answer/id #uuid "50f72eff-980c-5d6b-bc19-dfa625820604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324636} {:answer/id #uuid "6699b8d5-c375-5917-8a45-ab199058df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324827} {:answer/id #uuid "9313c2e6-4978-5466-83ec-9afb5f029598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325220} {:answer/id #uuid "dbdb866a-5a0b-5141-8de8-88e091ddbf5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9313c2e6-4978-5466-83ec-9afb5f029598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325220} :answer-field/id #uuid "51388a81-fbd8-54d3-b307-b0098d6fa5e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02ff2794-de30-53c1-a133-ec1abbd3f0b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-40208" :question/problem "Evaluate the triple integral \n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,dV\n$$\n\nwhere the region $R$ is given by\n\n$$\nR=\\{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,0\\le x\\le z\\sqrt{3}\\},\n$$\n\nand $D$ is a finite region in $yz$-plane enclosed between the $y$-axes, the line $y=2$ and the line $z=y$ in the first quadrant." :question/worked-solution "Writing down our triple integral as a mixed integral, we obtain\n\n$$\n{∭}_{R}2y\\,\\text{d}V={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA.\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{z\\sqrt{3}}2y\\,dx]dA & ={∬}_{D}2y[x]_{x=0}^{x=z\\sqrt{3}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now evaluate the double integral above over the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](images/63/63a8768b2769fad339ba7667357812d2dda0ea856e846ad666a100f8bc1336e9.png)\n\nWe can evaluate our double integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2yz\\sqrt{3}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2z\\,dz]dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=y}dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}y\\sqrt{3}({y}^{2}-0)\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}\\,dy \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{[\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(\\frac{16}{4}-0) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133915 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0bd48398-cb9d-579f-b7f7-0f6be19172ce" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Mixed Integral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "187c8796-6dc3-5960-ad59-8f0656a81c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324184} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa9da1c-2f67-5afd-a97d-d08f1c77a175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324309} {:answer/id #uuid "5c500570-ff2b-5461-8af9-215bc4a13b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324737} {:answer/id #uuid "bc366c6d-9415-56cd-8b14-c097e136ed07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325587} {:answer/id #uuid "c383f917-f536-517b-85d8-8b37b247c1e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325653}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "187c8796-6dc3-5960-ad59-8f0656a81c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324184} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e33ce57-aff2-5219-aafd-65b47610eecd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326475}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df0fc1c3-daea-50ab-b3dc-d1aac4fefd9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40395" :question/problem "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $yz$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD=\\{(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 4-{y}^{2}\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $x,$ treating $y$ and $z$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{y}12z\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{D}12z[x]_{x=0}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12z(y-0)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}12yz\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}yz\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{y}^{2}}12yz\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=4-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}6y(4-{y}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(96y-48{y}^{3}+6{y}^{5})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[48{y}^{2}-12{y}^{4}+{y}^{6}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =48(2)^{2}-12(2)^{4}+(2)^{6} \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
